tyler tony and his dude perfect co-stars  are known for creative trick shots and  absurd dares but did you know tony has  also saved rhinos and shattered world  records keep watching to learn more  about youtube's favorite bearded  renaissance man the dude perfect team  spends a lot of their time competing  against each other in what they call  battles which are based on the original  competitions that spawned the channel  these can be anything from demolition  derby to a giant version of pictionary  according to the official dude perfect  wiki tony has the most battle wins out  of the entire dude perfect ensemble cast  with 26 solo battle wins he currently  has a 12 win lead on any of his other  castmates the battle videos are some of  the highest viewed videos on their main  youtube channel with their most recent  airsoft battle video amassing over 12  million views in under 4 months in  addition to the sports based  competitions tony has also performed  well in the dude perfect overtime  segments will unfortunate and cool not  cool first and foremost tony is an avid  hunter and fisherman there are pictures  of him all over his instagram with fish  ducks turkeys geese and larger game from  reading some of the descriptions on  these posts it appears as though he does  his due diligence as far as getting  permits sticking to quotas and generally  respecting the local wildlife he also  seems to work hard at passing down these  practices to his children in a  responsible way in addition to hunting  tony participates in animal conservation  efforts as well as recently as may of  2021 he traveled with the dude perfect  crew to south africa and participated in  some rhino rescue with the rhino 9-1-1  organization in total they helped  tranquilize five animals so that  veterinarians could get close enough to  treat them for injuries sustained from  illegal poachers it seems that some of  these efforts may be having a positive  effect as some species of rhino in south  africa are rising in numbers and getting  closer to being taken off of the  critically endangered list according to  the world wildlife fund social media has  been picking apart the dude perfect  videos for years accusing them of using  cgi and other tricks in order to fake  their shots it got so heated at one  point that the group did an interview on  the today show to address the  controversy and they emphatically  repeated that they do not fake their  trick shots in any way obviously that  won't stop people from leveling  criticism at the group but tony doesn't  seem very bothered by this in fact when  people first started questioning the  veracity of their videos he took the  criticism in stride if people are  thinking that there's no way it could  actually be done in real life then we're  obviously doing something right after  such a wide array of success it's hard  to say exactly how much tony is worth  he's been collaborating for years with  his four other youtube partners which  means that his net worth is  intrinsically tied in with theirs even  when trying to guess how much the group  as a whole is worth the numbers can vary  according to celebrity net worth tony  could be worth around 10 million dollars  assuming the channel's net worth is  evenly split among the cast members  other websites such as wealthy gorilla  suggest a more conservative group net  worth of 30 million dollars but that's  nothing to sneeze at the dude perfect  group aren't just wasting their money on  frivolous purchases either all five cast  members are pretty charitable with tony  being far from the exception in addition  to flying to south africa to help  endangered species he's joined his  professional partners in donating to  organizations like charity water  compassion international and even the  make-a-wish foundation from charity to  trick shots it's no secret that the dude  perfect guys love taking their  challenges to the next level especially  when world records are involved  currently tony reigns supreme as a  four-time guinness world record holder  just on his own not even counting the  group awards that they have all earned  collectively his first award was won on  january 23 2017 when tony threw a  football into a basketball hoop from 50  yards away he added a second world  record to his resume the very next day  after successfully throwing another  football through a hoop from over 99  feet in the air the following year tony  set a particularly slimy world record  when he crushed 45 eggs with his toes in  30 seconds in 2019 he won himself  another award plaque for successfully  slicing 66 lemons and limes in 30  seconds for one of their overtime  segments as of spring 2022 none of these  records have been surpassed by any  challengers and it should be interesting  to see what sorts of records he and his  buddies try to set in the future  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  your favorite stuff are coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one  [Music]
 

